                  <provenance type="#g"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_122">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St
                        Paul)</orgName><p>On verso of last leaf is written <q>Psalterium Radulphi
                           glosatum d.ii. gradus i</q>. The second folio of the proemium, on the
                        verso of which was doubtles the Beatus page of the Psalter, is missing. Fol.
                        1 ends <q>per[suasione]</q>.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><q>Christopheri Materas</q> (verso of last
                     leaf). Compare Bodleian Summary Catalogue 2715.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bought by <persName>C. H. St J.
                        Hornby</persName> in 1911 from Ludwig Rosenthal of Munich. From Hornby it
                     passed to <persName>E. G. Millar</persName> (1877–1966) (under whose name it is
                     recorded in the first and second editions of MLGB). Millar bequeathed his
                     manuscripts to the British Library. Millar Bequest III.</provenance>
               </history>
